{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507585-tecnocracy-reactions","id":1507585,"title":"Tecnocracy Reactions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-06T09:10:29-07:00","id":1507585,"title":"Tecnocracy Reactions","content":"It's a point that got me thinking and feel free to correct me if I'm wrong, but from what I could understand, the goal of the Technocracy is to ensure that the foundation of the world is science to prevent a possible threat from the wizards since if it weren't for the paradox they could theoretically do absolutly everything and so I think that perhaps it would also be in their interest to deal with the other supernaturals, since if they were seen by the mortals they could change their perception of the supernatural, apart from what would happen due to the shock of interests. Some examples that came to mind were:<br /> <br /> - In case a vampire hinders the Syndicate economically, this is because they already say they control the world economy so this could create a problem for the Syndicate if they suddenly decide to move that money or the vampire disappears and the economy goes into chaos.<br /> <br /> - In case a Technocracy member is a kinfolk and therefore has limited knowledge from werewolves, how would they react? Would they try to establish relationships? Would they experiment on the kinfolk in order to explain the powers of the Fera? Would they think of ways to deal with them?<br /> <br /> - I couldn't think of anything directly with the Changelings, but I thought in the case of an animated chimera, normally they can't be seen by common mortals, but there are exceptions, how would they act in point of it, they would distrust magic at first , but they wouldn't be constrained by the paradox so I believe that would create some suspicion.<br /> <br /> - A fallen one could found a cult and make a suspicious demonstration of their powers what could be mistaken for magic, how they would react to it, they control the media, but not enough in today's world, where everyone has a cell phone, I imagine.<br /> <br /> - An interesting point would be their reaction in case of information leakage, I think that even having enviable security, it would not be totally impenetrable, so a very skilled Nosferatu or GW hackers could find a breach and steal information and maybe pass it on for others. What would the effects of that be? Technocracy would have to shred somehow or create a smokescreen.<br /> <br /> - In case they find any Fera, more specifically those that were artificially created by Pentex, the Monckering beasts, how would they react? I imagine they could eventually find out from tests that they were conceived in the lab, and even find a connection with Pentex, even more so if you consider the influence that Pentex has in the world and even being a business partner.<br /> <br /> - This is even unlikely, but what if they were discovered by hunters and in the worst case by the SI, the technocrats do not see themselves as wizards, but these groups may not see it that way, how would the reaction be?<br /> <br /> Just to clarify that I'm aware that the general policy for all these conflicts is to ignore the other groups as they're not direct opponents and balance issues and all that, but I still think those are valid points to think about.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T22:20:18-07:00","id":1507656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507585-tecnocracy-reactions#post1507585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- In case a Technocracy member is a kinfolk and therefore has limited knowledge from werewolves, how would they react? Would they try to establish relationships? Would they experiment on the kinfolk in order to explain the powers of the Fera? Would they think of ways to deal with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>What will happen does depend on what kind of Technocrats we are talking about, and what choices and decisions they make usually, and what they have done recently.<br /> <br /> I think that in this case there would be no exploitative, disrespectful, or radical plans, experimentation, or tests.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy from the current supplements is not as hostile or antagonistic as they might have appeared in for example first edition of MtA. <br /> <br /> In order to consider what might have in a particular situation, more specific aims, ambitions, and goals would need to be outlined and defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}